From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 17:06:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 239/240] patch 0239 -- Campaign 3 GUS P2 (#28): Pixtone SFX on
 GF1 voices

Renders the 117 Pixtone .pxt and uploads them (8-bit unsigned mono @ 22050 Hz)
into the Gravis Ultrasound's on-board DRAM once at init, then plays them on the
GF1's hardware voices alongside the native GM music -- the AUDIO_BACKEND=gus
path is now music+SFX, not music-only.

Why DOS needs this: unlike a DAC-less AdLib card, the GUS has its own DAC + 1MB
sample RAM, so Cave Story's digital SFX render on the GF1 too. No SDL3_mixer
exists on the no-SB GUS path, so the SFX go out-of-band like the music:
- Pixtone::initGusSfx renders + sign-flips (xor 0x80 -> GF1 8-bit unsigned) +
  SDL_DOSGusUploadSample each .pxt to a persistent low-DRAM band.
- A THIRD Pixtone::play/playResampled branch (_gusPlay) allocates a GF1 voice
  from the SHARED driver pool (the same SDL_DOSGusAllocVoice pool the music
  note path uses), sets freq (22050*percent/100) / vol / center pan, starts it
  one-shot (loop-enable for ambient loopers). Wave-ended voices reaped via
  voice_active_mask; pool exhaustion drops the SFX (music protected).
- MidiBackendGus::on_song_start auto-snapshots dram_used at first song start as
  the SFX keep-mark, so SDL_DOSGusResetDram(keep) preserves the SFX bank across
  per-song .pat residency swaps.
- SoundManager gus path calls initGusSfx (no MIX_CreateTrack) + the playSfx/
  stopSfx no-op gates revert for gus (only adlib stays music-only).

SFX dispatch is main-loop context (playSfx is game-logic-driven), so no engine
DPMI lock; the driver's shared-pool ops must be IRQ-safe (music note_on calls
AllocVoice from the PIT IRQ). Built clean; two-witness embeds the gus SFX
banners + GF1 voice exports; no pcspk. Full series re-applies (0238 -> 0239).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
